  partName: Engine Block
  description: The Engine Block is a tiny, thin-flat component positioned at the
    middle-center-center of the engine, serving as the main structural component
    of the engine. Made of danmen material, it provides excellent strength-to-weight
    ratio and thermal conductivity, and its compact size allows for minimal engine
    size and weight. Notably, the Engine Block is the foundation of the engine, housing
    the cylinders, crankshaft, and other critical components.
